# Response headers for everything served from Workers Static Assets (the SPA
# shell, JS, CSS, fonts, images). API responses get their own headers from
# src/worker/index.ts. Keep the two in sync when adding origins.
#
# style-src allows inline styles because UI primitives position popovers with
# style attributes. challenges.cloudflare.com serves the Turnstile widget
# (script and frame) when bot protection is enabled.
# Third-party analytics is not loaded on account, invitation, or content routes.
#
# Cloud import pickers (M16, PLAN.md §9). Each is offered only when its keys are
# configured, but the CSP allowances are static, so they are always present:
# - Google Drive: script apis.google.com + accounts.google.com (Picker loader +
#   GIS), frame docs.google.com + accounts.google.com (Picker UI + GIS iframe),
#   connect www.googleapis.com + accounts.google.com (Drive media download +
#   token). Picker thumbnails load inside the docs.google.com frame, governed by
#   Google's CSP, so img-src is unchanged.
# - Dropbox: script + frame www.dropbox.com (dropins.js Chooser + its relay
#   iframe, and the PKCE sign-in popup target), connect *.dropboxusercontent.com
#   (the Chooser's temporary direct link, and any redirect hop, which CSP
#   re-checks) plus api.dropboxapi.com (PKCE token) and content.dropboxapi.com
#   (files/upload for save-to-cloud).
# - OneDrive: no external script (MSAL is bundled); frame login.microsoftonline.com
#   (MSAL silent-renew iframe); connect login.microsoftonline.com +
#   graph.microsoft.com (token + Graph browse/save) plus the download and upload
#   hosts, which differ by account type: *.files.1drv.com / *.up.1drv.com and
#   my.microsoftpersonalcontent.com (personal), *.sharepoint.com and
#   tenant-my.sharepoint.com (work/school), already covered by *.sharepoint.com.
# Every other script stays self-hosted. Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy is relaxed to
# same-origin-allow-popups because all three pickers hand their result back
# through a popup's window.opener, which a bare same-origin policy severs.
# Tracked in PLAN.md §9.
#
# No upgrade-insecure-requests: production is HTTPS-only behind HSTS, every
# source list here is 'self' or an explicit https origin, and an https page
# cannot load http subresources under this policy anyway. WebKit (Safari) also
# applies the directive to plain-http localhost, which Chromium exempts, so the
# directive made the local preview unrenderable in the iPhone test projects.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://apis.google.com https://accounts.google.com https://www.dropbox.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://www.googleapis.com https://accounts.google.com https://*.dropboxusercontent.com https://api.dropboxapi.com https://content.dropboxapi.com https://login.microsoftonline.com https://graph.microsoft.com https://*.files.1drv.com https://*.up.1drv.com https://my.microsoftpersonalcontent.com https://*.sharepoint.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://docs.google.com https://accounts.google.com https://www.dropbox.com https://login.microsoftonline.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin-allow-popups
